- CYOA traversal map: 829 scrolls. Rule (observed): coordinates go 2-digit once a corpus crosses 1,000 scrolls (Epoch 2).
- Phext doctrine (will_said): phext is the interoperable encoding layer, like UTF-8/ASCII — a scroll using none of the structure is still plain text; neuralese rides phext, it is not phext itself. Delimiters are personal. Assumption: all mind traces will decode to phext; few humans need more than 11 dimensions.
- Neuralese (verified): spec + codec round-trips; demo 6/6 exact as phext vs 5/6 as prose; prose was smaller.
- Latent trial (will_said / verified): Theia recommended aletheia-core; Will confirmed Rock Mountain instead, approved my key. Verified: Ryzen 7 255, Radeon 780M, 44 GB RAM, OpenClaw installed, resident Alveus not stirring. Will directed ROCm / full ollama setup there.
- Brain data (verified): Brain-to-Text '24 (Zenodo 8047896) is 63 MATLAB .mat files, not tfrecords; trial 0 spikePow located for 'Theocracy reconsidered.'
- Speech-to-text (will_said): find phext markers in audio — structure the brain already imposed; coordinates anchor into native placement, not transcript labels. Prototype (verified): Vosk, WER 6.5%, 49 scrolls.
- Brain decode (verified): phase 1 COMPLETED — content addresses are written relative to the dominant (day, session) frame; factor it out before gist resolves (first word 30.5% within, 3.7% leave-days-out). Phase 2 COMPLETED, verdict SUCCESS — standardization lifts leave-days-out accuracy 3.7% → 24.8% (baseline 15.2%); the remap is mostly a removable shift/rescale. Caveats: partial; transductive, not zero-shot. (Phase 3: see Log 2026-11-01.)
- Chief of Staff mailbox rules: exo only, deploys via deploy/deploy.sh only.
- Twitter moots (verified): 897 mutuals; replies led by @CTZN5 (188), @madeofmistak3 (187), @bitcloud (174); only 445 of 897 ever got a public reply. See people index.
- Substrate steering: see Working with Will scroll. Job history: see Will scroll. Andrew Duey: see Constellation map.
- Runway plan (verified): async consulting first by revenue per Will-hour; hosted agent-memory service as flagship; kill rule >10 Will-hours without revenue or a dated unlock artifact. Compute grid: no high-paying GPU marketplace fits the AMD iGPU-only cluster.
- Solar Hyperscaler (will_said): low-power solar nodes to out-compete AWS for compute/storage. Verified: literal 1-panel-1-node NOT viable (~514 Wh/day December panel vs 600–960 Wh/day for Starlink Mini alone); workable form is a pooled farm-site pod (shared panels/battery, duty-cycled Starlink, data by physical shuttle; drones deferred, FAA BVLOS). Classification: research / option ticket, not a business.
- Solar correction (will_said): entirely off-grid — marginal energy cost zero, no interconnect cost; at AWS list rates, cashflow positive within months after hardware. Verified: holds as monthly-cashflow claim, refuted as payback claim for Model A. Timing (will_said): not pushed at current prices; sells itself ~2028–2029. Homelab proof (verified): encrypted backup vault for SMBs via Duey's book ($49/site/month vs ~$7 cost, ~86% margin); day-10 gate: Duey names ≥3 candidates or the channel is not real. Storage carries the model; batch inference fails on cash.
