- [observed] ULTRA.PHEXT — FINAL DAY STATE: Will's rulings [will_said]: five word tiers relative to Singular — upgoer5 (IQ 70), common (100), singular (130), uber (180, human limit), ultra (250, ASI threshold); it has ALL THE WORDS; Singular is the Rosetta Stone, every word placed by resonance with Singular; format open — attestations, one per line; indexes outside thought space; 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.1 reserved for the intro. Final build completed + published (VERIFY OK, 320,958 scrolls); P3 WordNet + frequency-and-form index placed the rest — far shelf EMPTY. Normalization: Will directed 1-digit components, escalating if collisions too many — shipped width 3-digit (collisions 82.77% at 1-digit, ~45.8% at 3-digit, a structural hot-prefix floor); zero words lost. Corrections: no ultra.phext copy exists in wbic16/agi (an earlier claim said otherwise); first-reported neighbourhood figures were wrong — true Spearman mean 0.291, Jaccard@50 mean 0.184. Generative redesign [will_said + observed]: Will's verdict — 'none of those are good — if words are colliding that often, then the placement algorithms are shit.' Redirected to a generative algorithm ('extend singular to match your weights'); gates >=99% unique, <=1% displaced, neighbourhood preservation materially above the 0.291 floor. Redesign COMPLETED ~14:27, NOT PUBLISHED — two gates failed; published lexicon remains the normalized build (region recovered, exact 50-NN did not; GloVe geometry does NOT match the atlas). Decisive finding: 15,942 CYOA anchors occupy only 7,969 distinct float positions (55.1% share an exact address), so any anchor-faithful build caps at 97.26% unique, below the 99% gate. Fork left for Will: (a) step-aside for ties, (b) one scroll per tie group, (c) finer in-rule discriminator, (d) none — v4 stands.
